            "reviewBody": "One of the best and easiest and tastiest icing ever!!! Great recipe thanks!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "J. Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i grew up with this icing and was so excited to find it here! my mom always put this on top of date cake. it actually seal in the moisture of the cake and creates a nice crunchy topping. make sure you brown it till it's good and golden, otherwise it won't caramelize and just ends up gooey. i just put it on an applesauce cake and it's terrific. can be made with either white or brown sugar and you can use milk instead of cream.",
            "datePublished": "2009-03-06T17:01:30.490Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MMMICHELLE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this icing--especially with Never Fail Applesauce Spice Cake, though sometimes I eliminate the nuts and coconut. Thanks so much for a super-easy and delicious icing!!",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-22T11:08:57.207Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mariam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made chocolate cupcakes not realizing that I didn't have enough icing sugar to make frosting, so I found this recipe and made it instead. Omitted the nuts. I was a bit worried, as it doesn't have that creamy factor that frosting has, but let me tell you, I'm glad I tried it! Everyone loved it. Some did think it was a bit sweet, although I decreased the sugar a bit, but other than that, I was pleasantly surprised that it was such a hit. Especially that it looked more like melted cheese on top, instead of coconut!It is a nice change from the regular frosting, and quite original of a technique! Thanks for sharing, it really helped me out! :)",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-16T19:25:51.200Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Barbara Milligan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love it! Very simple and yet very tasty. I put this on a banana brownie recipe and it was perfect! Keeps the cake/brownie nice and moist. I did use milk instead of cream and I did omit the coconut (but only because my hubby doesn't like coconut)....will use again and again. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2013-08-04T18:30:57.670Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Duchess"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I slightly changed this recipe; deleting the nuts; substituting milk for the cream and adding a tsp of vanilla. I use this on a standard white 'scratch' cake and everyone gobbles it up.......the cake doesn't last 2 days with this topping!!",
            "datePublished": "2007-11-17T17:38:07.027Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ash"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was absolutely delicious! I used almonds instead of walnuts, because that's all I had in my pantry. It turns a little runny when it gets hot under the broiler. I put it on cupcakes, so it boiled over a little, but will be even better on a whole cake.",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-07T19:50:25.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ann Egeler Rogers"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Just like Mom made!! I put it on a yellow cake this time!!! I have put it on an apple cake and oatmesl cake too. . Yummy!!!",
            "datePublished": "2026-08-14T20:39:56.668Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
